-- Demo quiz: 5 fixed questions per domain (75 in all), chosen from the existing bank and approved.
-- Generated by scripts/generate-submodule-seed-sql.ts. Matches rows by domain and exact question text. Safe to re-run;
-- it only fills empty demo positions. Change picks later in Admin > Question bank (Demo position).

with pick(track, domain, pos, question) as (values
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Prompting and Task Execution$q$, 1, $q$A marketing coordinator types "Write something about our new product." The first draft is generic. Which change would most improve the next result?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Prompting and Task Execution$q$, 2, $q$Claude's first draft of a client update is accurate but far too formal. What is the most effective next step?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Prompting and Task Execution$q$, 3, $q$An operations lead wants Claude to turn 40 pages of meeting notes into a risk register, a stakeholder email and a one-page summary. What is the best approach?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Prompting and Task Execution$q$, 4, $q$A team wants Claude to draft a customer email and also to analyse survey data for trends. How should the prompts differ?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Prompting and Task Execution$q$, 5, $q$A finance analyst wants a quarterly variance commentary built from four data exports. Which approach gives the most reliable result?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Output Evaluation and Validation$q$, 1, $q$You asked Claude for a comparison of three vendors across price, support and security. The response covers price and support only. What should you do?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Output Evaluation and Validation$q$, 2, $q$Claude summarises a market report and states that a competitor's revenue grew 38% last year. The figure will go into a board deck. What should you do first?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Output Evaluation and Validation$q$, 3, $q$Which of these are common warning signs that a Claude response may contain a hallucination? Select 2.$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Output Evaluation and Validation$q$, 4, $q$A finance analyst wants Claude's output to be pasted into a spreadsheet with consistent columns. Which output request works best?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Output Evaluation and Validation$q$, 5, $q$A team uses Claude to draft responses to customer complaints. Which situation most clearly requires a human to review before sending?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Product and Model Selection$q$, 1, $q$A support team needs thousands of short, routine reply drafts per day, where speed and cost matter most. Which approach fits best?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Product and Model Selection$q$, 2, $q$Which statement best describes how the Claude model tiers are generally positioned?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Product and Model Selection$q$, 3, $q$A consultant needs to produce a polished, shareable interactive dashboard from a data summary and iterate on its layout. Which Claude capability is the best fit?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Product and Model Selection$q$, 4, $q$A legal team needs Claude to analyse a complex contract for subtle conflicts between clauses. Quality matters far more than speed. Which choice fits best?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Product and Model Selection$q$, 5, $q$A long conversation with Claude has drifted and earlier instructions seem to be ignored. What is the most sensible action?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Workflow Integration and Solution Design$q$, 1, $q$A manager asks where Claude could help in the customer-onboarding process. What is the best first step?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Workflow Integration and Solution Design$q$, 2, $q$A team reviews weekly status reports by hand. Which use of Claude best augments the workflow while keeping accountability clear?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Workflow Integration and Solution Design$q$, 3, $q$A team has a repetitive weekly reporting task that always follows the same steps and input format. How should it design the solution?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Workflow Integration and Solution Design$q$, 4, $q$Which tasks are good candidates for using Claude to support planning and research? Select 2.$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Workflow Integration and Solution Design$q$, 5, $q$You are presenting a Claude pilot to senior stakeholders. Which message is the most credible?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Configuration and Knowledge Management$q$, 1, $q$A sales team asks Claude similar questions about the same product documents every week. Which setup saves the most effort?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Configuration and Knowledge Management$q$, 2, $q$A Project's knowledge includes a pricing sheet that changed last month. Users now receive outdated prices. What is the right fix?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Configuration and Knowledge Management$q$, 3, $q$Which custom instruction is the most effective for a Project that drafts customer emails?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Configuration and Knowledge Management$q$, 4, $q$Users report that a Project's answers contradict each other. Two versions of the same policy document are in its knowledge. What is the best fix?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Configuration and Knowledge Management$q$, 5, $q$Which Project instruction is most useful for a team that needs consistent answers about an internal HR policy?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Governance, Risk, and Responsible Use$q$, 1, $q$Which is an appropriate use of Claude in a marketing team?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Governance, Risk, and Responsible Use$q$, 2, $q$An analyst wants Claude's help drafting a letter to a specific patient and has the patient's record open. What is the most appropriate approach?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Governance, Risk, and Responsible Use$q$, 3, $q$Your organisation has an approved-tools list and a rule against pasting client confidential data into unapproved services. A colleague suggests using a personal account to move faster. What should you do?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Governance, Risk, and Responsible Use$q$, 4, $q$A user asks Claude to write a convincing message that pretends to be the company's CEO asking staff for gift cards. How should this be handled?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Governance, Risk, and Responsible Use$q$, 5, $q$A team notices that Claude's drafted candidate summaries consistently describe one group more negatively. What is the most responsible response?$q$),
  ($q$associate$q$, $q$Troubleshooting and Optimization$q$, 1, $q$A reviewer says Claude's drafts are too long. What is the best adjustment?$q$),
